From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] waydroid-init: Detect Halium by a populated /vendor_extra

BOARD_ROOT_EXTRA_FOLDERS puts an empty /vendor_extra into every system
image, so the existence check made waydroid-init take every container
for a Halium one and skip GPU detection: on a mainline host the minigbm
allocator never started, mapper 4 was missing, and SurfaceFlinger
aborted with "Failed to create a valid texture". The host's vendor is
bind-mounted there only for Halium vendors, so test for a non-empty
directory instead.
---
 waydroid-init/main.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/waydroid-init/main.cpp b/waydroid-init/main.cpp
index 0b063c8..e810fc0 100644
--- a/waydroid-init/main.cpp
+++ b/waydroid-init/main.cpp
@@ -50,8 +50,9 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     base::SetProperty("waydroid.init.start", "1");
 
     // On Halium-based setups the device provides its own GPU/EGL/gralloc
-    // stack through vendor blobs (marked by the presence of /vendor_extra)
-    if (filesystem::exists("/vendor_extra")) {
+    // stack through vendor blobs, mounted on /vendor_extra. The directory
+    // itself is in every system image (BOARD_ROOT_EXTRA_FOLDERS).
+    if (!filesystem::is_empty("/vendor_extra", error) && !error) {
         Log::info("Halium vendor (/vendor_extra) detected; skipping GPU auto-detection");
         base::SetProperty("waydroid.init.done", "1");
         return 0;
